$DATUM 4-(3,4- dimethylphenoxy)-1-nitrobenzene was prepared from
3,4-dimethylphenol (3 g, 11 mmol), 1-fluoro-4-nitrobenzene (1.4 g, 10
mmol), and K2CO3 (1.5 g, 11 mmol) in 20 mL of DMF. A yellow solid was
obtained in 95% yield (2.3 g, 9.5 mmol). 4-(3,4-
dimethylphenoxy)-1-nitrobenzene, yield (2.3 g, 95%) 1H NMR (CDCl3; 400
MHz): δ 2.28 (s, 6), 6.81-6.88 (m, 2H), 6.96-7.00 (m, 2H), 7.17-7.19 (m,
1H), 8.16-8.20 (m, 2H). MS (ESI, pos. ion) m/z: 244 (M + 1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
