$DATUM 872-50-4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Biaryl ether (4). To a 100-gal reactor were charged
4-bromophenyl methyl sulfone 5 (15.45 kg, 65.7 mol), potassium phosphate
(28 kg, 132 mol), NMP (29 kg), and 4-trifluoromethoxyphenol 2 (12.05 kg,
67.6 mol). The heterogeneous mixture was heated to an internal
temperature of 145 ± 15 °C for 8 h. The reaction mixture was cooled to 25
°C, and water (~46 kg) was added over 10 min to quench the reaction. The
internal temperature increased to ~39 °C as the solid phophate salts
dissolved. The remaining water (~46 kg) was added slowly (over 1 h); in
this case, after ~60% of the water had been added (temp at 32 °C) the
product began to crystallize from the mixture. Following the water
addition, the mixture was stirred while cooling to ambient temperature.
The product was collected by filtration. The filter cake was washed with
water until the eluant was neutral by pH test strips. The cake was dried
by suction and then transferred to a vacuum oven and dried (at ~100 mmHg
with nitrogen bleed at <45 °C) to provide 4, 20.85 kg, (95% yield, 100%
potency vs a standard): Biaryl ether (4). Yield 20.85 kg, (95%) mp 74-75
°C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.90 (d, J = 9.1 Hz, 2H), 7.26 (br d, J =
9.2 Hz, 2H), 7.09 (d, J = 8.9 Hz, 4H), 3.06 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 161.4, 153.0, 134.5, 129.5, 122.7, 121.4, 121.1, 118.9, 117.7,
44.9. IR (KBr) 1589, 1503, 1274, 1245, 1148, 961, 837, 763 cm-1; MS
(APCI) 350 [M + NH4]+. Anal. Calcd for C14H11F3O4S: C, 50.60; H, 3.34; F,
17.15; O, 19.26; S, 9.65. Found: C, 50.49; H, 3.22; F, 17.31; S, 10.22.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM pilot plant, optimized for base, solvent, aryl halide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The Development of a Large-Scale Synthesis of Matrix Metalloproteinase
Inhibitor, ABT-518
