$DATUM 4-(4-tert-butylphenoxy)benzophenone, Figure 7. A Flame dried microwave
vial equipped with a stir bar under a blanket of argon was charged with
Cu-Ni/C (100 mg, 8 mol % Cu), Cs2CO3 (651 mg, 1.2 equiv),
1,10-phenanthroline (90 mg, 0.5 equiv), 4- bromobenzophenone (261 mg, 1
equiv), 4-tert-butylphenol (300 mg, 2 equiv) and dioxane (3 mL). The
mixture was vigorously stirred before it was placed in the microwave
reactor and heated to 200 °C for 3600 seconds. Upon cooling, the reaction
mixture was filtered through Celite®, solvents removed and the column
chromatography with 8% EtOAc in hexanes yielded product as a colorless
oil in 95% yield (314 mg). Spectral data matched those previously
reported for this compound.11 4-(4-tert-butylphenoxy)benzophenone, yield
(314 mg, 95%)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
