$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(2-Bromophenoxy)-benzonitrile (1a). 2-Bromophenol (2.11 mL, 20.0 mmol),
2-fluorobenzonitrile (2.17 mL, 20.0 mmol) and freshly ground K2CO3 (4.14
g, 30.0 mmol) were stirred in DMF (15 mL) at 100°C under N2 for 48 hours.
At rt sat. NH4Cl (50 mL) was added. Extraction with Et2O (5×50 mL) and
the combined organic phases were washed with brine (50 mL). Drying
(Na2SO4) and evaporation of the solvent gave the crude product which was
purified by FC (Heptane/EtOAc) yielding 5.20 g (95 %) of 1a as colorless
crystals. mp 77-78 °C (Heptane/EtOAc), Rf (Heptane/EtOAc 4:1) 0.38.
1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): 6.67 (dd, 1H, J=8.5, 0.5 Hz), 7.11-7.19 (m, 3H),
7.37 (td, 1H, J=7.8,1.6 Hz), 7.46 (ddd, 1H, J=8.5, 7.5, 1.7 Hz),
7.65-7.71 (m, 2H). 13C-NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): 103.1 (s), 115.7 (d), 115.8
(s), 115.9 (s), 122.5 (d), 122.8 (d), 126.9 (d), 129.0 (d), 134.0 (d),
134.20 (d), 134.23 (d), 151.4 (s), 159.1 (s). Anal. Calcd. for C13H8BrNO:
C, 56.96; H, 2.94; N, 5.11. Found: C, 56.94; H, 2.86, N, 4.93.
