$DATUM 6,7-Di[(3,5-di-tert-butyl)phenoxy]-2,3-dicyanonaphthalene (7). 3.36 g of
526 (10 mmol), 4.55 g of 3,5-di-tert-butylphenol (22 mmol), and 11 g of
K2CO3 (80 mmol) were mixed together in DMF (60 mL) under argon and heated
at 100 °C for 7 h (the completion of the reaction was followed with
thin-layer chromatography using dichloromethane as solvent). The mixture
was cooled till room temperature and then stirred upon addition of 0.4 L
of ice water. After 1 h of stirring, the white-yellowish solid was
collected and washed again with water. The compound was dried in a vacuum
at 70 °C overnight. Recrystallization from ethanol gave 5.5 g of 7 (94%).
6,7-Di[(3,5-di-tert-butyl)phenoxy]-2,3-dicyanonaphthalene (7). Yield 5.5
g (94%). MS (EI, 70 eV): 586.8 [M+], 561.8 [M+ - CN]. 1H NMR (CDCl3, δ):
1.30 (br, 36H, C(CH3)3), 6.74 (d, 4H, H-7), 7.30 (t, 2H, H-9), 7.72 (s,
2H, H-4), 8.55 (s, 2H, H-2). 13C NMR (CDCl3): 29.7, 29.9 (CH3), 35.3,
(C-tBu), 105.1, (C-1), 113.4 (CN), 120.0 (C- 4), 121.2.0 (C-3), 124.7,
(C-2), 127.4 (C-7), 138.0 (C-5), 148.7 (C-8), 153.0 (C-6).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
