$DATUM 3-Chloro-4-(4-methoxyphenoxy)benzonitrile (14a): A mixture of
p-hydroxyanisole (0.496g, 4 mmol), 3-chloro-4-fluoro-benzonitrile
(0.622g, 4 mmol) and K2CO3 (0.829g, 6 mmol) in MeCN (40 mL) was refluxed
overnight. After cooling down to room temperature the reaction mixture
was poured into water and extracted with CH2Cl2. The resulting organic
layers were dried over MgSO4 and evaporated under reduced pressure,
yielding the title compound which was pure enough for further use
according to NMR analysis. White crystalline solid, yield (0.980 g, 94%).
1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 7.72 (d, 1H, J=2 Hz), δ 7.41 (dd, 1H, J1=9 Hz,
J2=2 Hz), δ 6.97 (m, 4H), δ 6.77 (d, 1H, J=9 Hz), δ 3.82 (s, 3H) ppm; 13C
NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz) δ 158.7, δ 157.6, δ 147.9, δ 134.5, δ 132.3, δ 124.7,
δ 121.9, δ 118.0, δ 117.1, δ 115.6, δ 106.5, δ 56.0 ppm; mp 92-93 °C
(Lit6: 93-94 °C ); HRMS calcd for [C14H10NO2Cl] 259.0400, found 259.0393.
