$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the reaction of 4-n-alkylphenoxides with
pentafluorobenzene. 60% (w/w) sodium hydride in mineral oil (1.1 equiv.)
was charged to a round-bottomed flask (100 ml) equipped with a magnetic
follower. The reaction vessel evacuated under high vacuum and back-filled
with argon three times to create an inert atmosphere. The sodium hydride
was washed with dry hexane (10 ml), which was removed using a syringe,
and replaced with dry THF (40 ml). The 4-n-alkylphenol (1.0 equiv.) was
dissolved in dry THF (10 ml), under an atmosphere of argon, and carefully
added to the sodium hydride mixture, with stirring, to produce sodium
4-n-alkylphenoxide and hydrogen gas. When the evolution of hydrogen gas
had stopped pentafluorobenzene (1.0 equiv.) was added to the microwave
vial and the reaction was heated to reflux for 48 hr, left to cool,
poured on to water (30 ml) and extracted with dichloromethane (3 × 30
ml). The combined extracts were washed with water (50 ml) and dried
(MgSO4). The mixture was filtered and the solvent removed in vacuo and
purified by column chromatography on silica gel using hexane as the
eluent. 3-(4-Ethylphenoxy)-1,2,4,5-tetrafluorobenzene (10) Reaction of
60% (w/w) sodium hydride in mineral oil (0.360 g, 9.00 mmol),
4-ethylphenol (1.000 g, 8.19 mmol) and pentafluorobenzene (1.376 g, 8.19
mmol). 3-(4-ethylphenoxy)-1,2,4,5- tetrafluorobenzene 10 (1.700 g, 94 %)
as a colourless oil. (Found: C, 62.32; H, 3.75. C14H10F4O requires C,
62.23; H, 3.73 %); 1H NMR (500 MHz; CDCl3): δ 1.25 (3H, t, 3 J HH 7.5, CH
3), 2.65 (2H, q, 3 J HH 7.5, CH 2), 6.92 (2H, dm, 3 J HH 8.5, 3'-H), 6.96
(1H, tt, 3 J HF 10.3, 4 J HF 7.2, 6-H), 7.17 (2H, dm, 3 J HH 8.5, 2'-H);
13C NMR (126 MHz; CDCl3): δ 15.85 (s, CH3), 28.28 (s, CH2), 101.88 (t, 2
J CF 23.0, 6-C), 115.68 (s, 2'-C), 129.28 (s, 3'-C), 134.89 (tt, 2 J CF
13.2, 3 J CF 3.8, 3-C), 139.96 (s, 4'-C), 141.85 (dddd, 1 J CF 250, 2 J
CF 14.8, 3 J CF 4.7, 4 J CF 2.5, Ar-C), 146.69 (dddd, 1 J CF 248, 2 J CF
12.3, 3 J CF 12.3, 4 J CF 4.2, Ar-C), 155.53 (s, 1'-C); 19F NMR (658 MHz;
CDCl3; CFCl3): δ -139.44 (2F, ddd, 3 J FF = 21.2, 3 J FH = 10.3, 5 J FF =
10.3, 1-CF and 5-CF), -154.68 (2F, ddd, 3 J FF = 21.2, J FH = 7.2, 5 J FF
= 10.3, 2-CF and 4-CF); m/z (EI+) 271 (M+, 6%), 270 (M+, 69), 255 (100),
137 (14), 89 (16), 77 (32), 51 (15).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
