$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2.3.2 Synthesis of 3,3'-(4,4'-sulfonyl bis(1,4-phenylene) bis (oxy))
dianiline (SBOD) Into a 100 mL, three-necked, round-bottomed flask
equipped with a Dean-Stark trap, a condenser, a nitrogen inlet tube, a
thermometer, an oil bath, and a magnetic stirrer was placed 0.01 mol
(2.87 g) of 4,4'-dichlorobenzophenone, 25 mL of dry NMP, and 15 mL of dry
toluene and 0.021 mol (2.51 g) of 3-aminophenol. Then 0.0315 mol (4.36 g)
of K2CO3 was added to the mixture and the reaction mixture was heated to
140 °C for 6 h with continuous stirring. The generated water was removed
from the reaction mixture by azeotropic distillation. The reaction
temperature was raised to 160 °C by removing more toluene, and kept at
the same temperature for 25 h. During this time, progress of the reaction
was monitored by thin-layer chromatography (TLC). The resulting reaction
mixture was cooled and poured into water. Then 100 mL of 3% NaOH was
added to the mixture. After filtration, the mixture was washed repeatedly
with a 3% NaOH solution and water. The obtained compound was dried in a
vacuum oven at 60 °C. Yield 94%. Elemental analysis: Calc: C 66.67; H
4.63; N 6.48, Found: C 66.49; H 4.49; N 6.62
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dean-Stark trap used
