$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of
bis(4-(4-nitro-2-(4,5-diphenyl-1H-imidazol-2-yl)phenoxy)phenyl)
hexafluoropropane (DNIFP) In a 250 mL round-bottomed two-necked flask
equipped with a condenser, a magnetic stirrer bar and a nitrogen gas
inlet tube, a mixture of 1.68 g (0.005 mol)
4,40-(hexafluoroisopropylidene) diphenol, 3.75 g (0.01 mol) (DPI), and
1.40 g (0.01 mmol) anhydrous potassium carbonate in 20 mL of dry DMAc was
refluxed at 120 °C for 12 h and then cooled. The mixture was then poured
into water and the precipitate was collected by filtration and
recrystallized from ethanol. The yield of the crude product was obtained.
Yield 4.70 g, 94 %. mp = 278-280 °C. FT-IR (KBr disk) at cm-1: 3484, 3378
(NH2), 3445 (N-H imidazole ring), 3049 (C-H aromatic), 1633 (C=N), 1598
(C=C), 1530, 1351 (NO2), and 1208 (C-O-C). 1H NMR (DMSO-d6, δ in ppm):
6.55 (distorted s, 2H, Ar-H), 7.04 (d, 4H, Ar-H, J= 8 Hz), 7.19-7.23 (m,
6H, Ar-H), 7.26-7.29 (m, 9H, Ar-H), 7.31-7.34 (m, 5H, Ar-H), 7.49 (d, 4H,
Ar-H, J= 8 Hz), 7.90 (d, 4H, Ar-H, J= 8 Hz), 9.98 (s, 2H, N-H imidazole
ring). Elemental analysis calculated for C57H36F6N6O6: C, 67.46 %; H,
3.55 %; N, 8.28 % and found: C, 67.39 %; H, 3.64 %; N, 8.25 %.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and characterization of novel poly(amide-ether)s bearing
imidazole pendants: study of physical and optical properties
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ghaemy, Mousa; Sharifi, Samaneh; Nasab, Seyed Mojtaba Amini; Taghavi,
Mehdi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Polymer Bulletin (Heidelberg, Germany) (2013), 70(4), 1125-1142

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME158 STEP1
