$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of (7) A round bottom flask was charged with a 2.37 g (5.0
mmol) sample of 6, a 2.15 g (6.0 mmol) sample of 3, 1.04 g (7.5 mmol) of
potassium carbonate. To this mixture was added 2 mL of DMAc and the
resulting solution was heated to 180 °C over the course of 4 hours under
a nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction mixture was diluted with
dichloromethane and washed with saturate NaCl water for three times to
remove DMAc and potassium carbonate. The organic layer was dried over
MgSO4, filtered, evaporated. The yellow residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica using a 1:4 n-hexane/dichloromethane mixture as
the eluent. The solvent was removed and the white solid was dried in
vacuo at 40 °C for 3 hours (3.83 g, 4.7 mmol, 94%). IR (KBr): 3096, 2960,
1589, 1499, 1486, 1319, 1288, 1237, 1151, 1107, 872, 834 cm-1. 1H NMR
(CDCl3, r.t.): δ 7.87-7.80 (m, 8H), 7.38 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.04-6.91
(m, 18H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 1.31 (s, 9H) ppm; 13C NMR (CDCl3, r.t.): δ 162.8,
162.2, 161.65, 161.63, 156.8, 152.3, 151.7, 148.0, 147.8, 135.9, 135.7,
134.9, 134.6, 129.79, 129.73, 129.71, 129.65, 129.61, 126.9, 121.8,
121.7, 119.7, 117.5, 117.4, 116.8, 115.1, 55.5, 34.4, 31.3 ppm. MS
(MALDI-ToF) m/z calcd for (C47H40O9S2) 812.9, found 835.5 [M + Na] +.
