$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.2. General procedure for the synthesis of
2-phenoxybenzaldehydes 7a-7h (GP2): phenol (2.2 mmol, 1.2 equiv) and
anhydrous K2CO3 (2.20 mmol, 304 mg, 1.2 equiv) were added to a solution
of 2-fluorobenzaldehyde (2.00 mmol, 212 μL, 1.0 equiv) in DMA (3 mL) and
the resulting reaction mixture was slowly heated to 170 °C. After
stirring at that temperature for 4 h and cooling to room temperature the
reaction mixture was poured into H2O (10 mL) and the aqueous layer was
extracted with DCM (3 x20 mL). After drying over MgSO4, filtration and
concentration in vacuo the residue was purified by FC (P/MTBE) to afford
the desired 2-phenoxybenzaldehyde. With phenol (207 mg, 2.20 mmol, 1.2
equiv). With metha-cresol (208 μL, 2.20 mmol, 1.2 equiv).
2-(m-Tolyloxy)benzaldehyde (7h) as a colorless oil, yield 394 mg, 1.86
mmol, 93%. IR (neat): 2858br w, 1690s, 1599s, 1576m, 1475s, 1455s, 1393m,
1273m, 1248s, 1217s, 1188m, 1154s, 1141m, 1097m, 1035w, 1001w, 935m,
839m, 785m, 760s, 689m, 656m, 620m. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, 300 K) δ =
10.52 (s, 1 H, CHO), 7.94 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1 H, CHarom), 7.55 - 7.47 (m, 1
H, CHarom), 7.27 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 1 H, CHarom), 7.18 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 1 H,
CHarom), 7.00 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1 H, CHarom), 6.95 - 6.85 (m, 3 H, CHarom),
2.36 (s, 3 H, CH3). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, 300 K) δ = 189.4 (CHO), 160.1
(C), 156.4 (C), 140.4 (C), 135.7 (CH), 129.8 (CH), 128.3 (CH), 126.9 (C),
125.1 (CH), 123.2 (CH), 120.0 (CH), 118.5 (CH), 116.3 (CH), 21.4 (CH3).
HRMS (ESI) m/z = 235.0730 calcd. for C14H12O2Na [M+Na]+, found: 235.0729.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cross Dehydrogenative Coupling via Base-Promoted Homolytic Aromatic
Substitution (BHAS): Synthesis of Fluorenones and Xanthones
