$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Synthesis of Diaryl Ethers: An oven-dried test
tube, which was equipped with a magnetic stir bar and fitted with a
teflon screw-cap, was charged with L8 (1.5-7.5 mol %), [(cinnamyl)PdCl]2
(0.5-2.5 mol %), K3PO4 (318 mg, 1.5 mmol), aryl halide (1.0 mmol) and
phenol (1.5 mmol). The vessel was evacuated and backfilled with argon
(this process was repeated a total of three times) after which toluene
and DME were added via syringe (the amount of solvent is specific to each
substrate). The solution was stirred at the specified temperature for 16
h after which it was cooled to rt and diluted with ethyl acetate, washed
with water, filtered through a pad of silica gel (eluted with diethyl
ether), and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude material was
purified by flash chromatography via the Biotage SP4.
4-(4-methoxyphenoxy)benzonitrile (1).10 Following the General Procedure,
a mixture of 4-bromobenzonitrile (182 mg, 1.0 mmol), 4-OH-anisole (186
mg, 1.5 mmol), L8 (1.5 mol %), [(C6H9)PdCl]2 (0.5 mol %), K3PO4 (318 mg),
toluene (0.6 mL) and DME (0.3 mL) was stirred at room temperature for 24
h. The crude product was purified via the Biotage SP4 (silica-packed 25 g
snap column; 0-25% EtOAc/hexanes) to provide the title compound as a
white solid (207 mg, 92%). mp = 109 - 110 °C (lit. 108 - 110 °C). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.57 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 7.01 (d, J = 9.1 Hz, 2H),
6.94 (dd, J = 9.0, 7.2 Hz, 4H), 3.82 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ:
162.6, 157.1, 147.9, 134.2, 121.9, 119.1, 117.2, 115.4, 105.4, 55.4 ppm.
IR (neat, cm-1): 2222, 1610, 1498, 1446, 1297, 1238, 1197, 1031, 848
cm-1. Anal. Calcd. for C14H11NO2: C, 74.65; H, 4.92. Found: C, 74.41; H,
4.71.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reaction conditions shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A New Biarylphosphine Ligand for the Pd-Catalyzed Synthesis of Diaryl
