$DATUM 3-Chloro-4-(2-hydroxy-6-methoxy-4-propylphenoxy)benzonitrile (30).
2,6-Dimethoxy-4-propylphenol (1.0 g, 5.1 mmol),
3-chloro-4-fluoro-benzonitrile (0.79 g, 5.1 mmol), and K2CO3 (1.41 g,
10.2 mmol) in DMSO (8 mL) were heated to 100 °C under nitrogen for 12 h
(method A above). Usual workup followed by purification of the crude
reaction mixture by column chromatography (SiO2, 10% EtOAc/hexanes)
afforded the compound
3-chloro-4-(2,6-dimethoxy-4-propylphenoxy)-benzonitrile (1.57 g, 93%).
3-chloro-4-(2,6-dimethoxy-4-propylphenoxy)-benzonitrile, yield (1.57 g,
93%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.00 (t, J= 7.3 Hz, 3H), 1.70 (quin, J=
7.5 Hz, 2H), 2.62 (t, J=7.5 Hz, 2H), 3.78 (s, 6H), 6.49 (s, 2H), 6.62 (d,
J=8.6 Hz, 1H), 7.38 (dd, J= 8.6, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 7.73 ppm (d, J= 1.8 Hz,
1H). 13C NMR(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 13.4, 24.2, 38.2, 55.8, 105.0, 114.5,
117.6, 122.8, 128.3, 131.5, 133.4, 141.4, 151.9, 157.6 ppm. MS (ESI) m/z:
354.1 [M + Na]+ .
