$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 4-(4-nitrophenoxy) phenol: NPP. 1-Fluoro-4-nitrobenzene
[1.439 g (0.01 mol)] and hydroquinone [1.11 g (0.01 mol)] were placed
into a two-necked, round-bottomed, 100-mL flask which was equipped with a
magnetic stirrer, nitrogen gas inlet tube, and Dean-Stark con-denser.
Then, 25 mL of dried NMP, 15 mL of dried toluene, and 1.396 g (0.01 mol)
of K2CO3 were added into the flask. The solution was heated to 140 °C for
6 h, followed by 165 °C for 20 h with continuous stirring. When the
reaction was completed, the resulting mixture was cooled and poured
slowly into 200 mL of distilled water in order to precipitate the
synthesized nitrophenol compound. Then the mixture was filtered, and the
product was collected by filtration, and dried in vacuum oven at 90 °C
for 15 h. (yield, 93 %). mp, 165-168 °C). [IR (KBr), ν (cm-1): 3,434 (O-H
stretching), 3,120 (C-H aromatic stretching), 1,505 (C═C aromatic
stretching), 1,484 and 1,342 (NO2 stretching), 1,326 (C-N stretching).
1H-NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6, δ, ppm, 25 °C): 9.55 (s, 1H, Ha), 8.20 (d, 2H,
He), 7.01 (d, 2H, Hc), 6.99 (d, 2H, Hd), 6.82 (d, 2H, Hb). Elem. Anal.
Calcd: (%) For C12H9NO4 (231 g mol-1): C, 62.34; H, 3.90; N, 6.06; Found:
C, 62.40; H, 3.93; N, 6.01].
