$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
{4-[η6-(2-Chlorophenyl)-η5-cyclopentadienyliron(II)]-piperazin-1-yl}methyl
Polystyrene Hexafluorophosphate (5a). Piperazin-1-yl methyl polystyrene
(4a) (24 g, 24.2 mmol), η6-dichlorobenzene-η5-cyclopentadienyliron(II)
hexafluorophosphate (2a) (25 g, 60.6 mmol), and potassium carbonate (13.4
g, 97.0 mmol) were suspended in dry THF (400 mL) and the solution was
stirred overnight at 60 °C. The resin was filtered, washed with THF (2 X
100 mL), H2O (2 X 100 mL), THF (2 X 100 mL), MeOH (2 X 100 mL), and
CH2Cl2 (3 X 100 mL) and dried in vacuo at 40 °C giving 32.9 g (99%) of 5a
as a red resin. Method B (SNAr with the sodium salt of phenols,
thiophenols, and alkylmercaptanes): A solution of sodium
2-methoxyphenolate (7, 0.70 M), sodium cyclohexyl-1-thiolate (8, 0.25 M),
sodium adamantane-1-thiolate (9, 0.25 M), and sodium
3-methoxy-benzenephenolate (10, 0.50 M) was prepared by adding
respectively 2-methoxyphenol, cyclohexanethiol, adamantane-1-thiol, or
3-methoxythiophenyl to sodium hydride (60% suspension in mineral oil) in
dry DMF at room temperature. [Caution: Generation of heat and hydrogen.]
The mixtures were stirred for an additional 30 min after gas generation
had ceased. The alcoholate/thiolate (11 mmol) was transferred to resins
5a, 5b, 5c, 5d, or 5e (3.0 g, 1.9-2.2 mmol), and DMF was added to a total
volume of 45 mL. The reactions were stirred at 70 °C for 16 h. The resins
were filtered, washed with DMF (2 x 50 mL), MeOH (2 x 50 mL), H2O (2 x 50
mL), MeOH (2 x 50 mL), and CH2Cl2 (3 x 50 mL), and dried in vacuo at 40
°C to give resins 16a-e, 17ad, 18a-e, and 19a-e, respectively. General
Method for Decomplexation of Resin-Bound Iron Complexes. Preparation of
1,10-phenanthroline solution (0.5 M) used for decomplexation: To
1,10-phenanthroline (180.0 g, 1.0 mol) was added under stirring in the
following order CH3CN (600 mL), H2O (200 mL), concentrated HCl (40 mL),
H2O (160 mL), CH3CN (900 mL), and finally H2O (approximately 100 mL)
until the solution became clear. Decomplexation on Solid Phase: The
resins 15a-e, 16a-e, 17a-d, 18a-e, 19a-e, 20a-e, 21a-e, 22a, and 23d were
suspended in a light-transparent reactor tube with the thus prepared
1,10-phenanthroline solution (10 mL/1 g of resin). The suspensions were
agitated under irradiation with visible light for 12 h. During this time,
the solution became intensely red. The resins were filtered and washed
with MeOH (3 x 50 mL), THF (3 x 50 mL), and MeOH (3 x 50 mL) until the
washing solution was colorless (approximately 5 cycles). The irradiation
procedure was repeated until decomplexation was complete (approximately 5
cycles). After complete decomplexation, the resins were washed with MeOH
(3 x 50 mL) and THF (3 x 50 mL) and suspended in a triethylamine solution
(1 M in THF) for 1 h. The resins were then further washed with MeOH (3 x
50 mL), CH2Cl2 (3 x 50 mL), MeOH (3 x 50 mL,) and CH2Cl2 (3 x 50 mL) and
dried in vacuo at 50 °C to yield resins 24a-e, 25a-e, 26a-d, 27a-e,
28a-e, 29a-e, 30a-e, 31a, and 32d. Standard Cleavage from Polymer
Support: 4-[2-(3-Methoxybenzyloxy)phenyl]piperazine-1-carboxylic Acid
Methyl Ester (33a). The procedure for a typical experiment follows. A
suspension of resin 24a (2.41 g, 2.00 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (30 mL)
was cooled to 0 °C and neat methyl chloroformate (25.0 mmol) was slowly
added. After 1 h of additional stirring at 0 °C, the temperature was
raised to room temperature, and the reaction mixture was stirred
overnight. The resin was filtered and washed with H2O (1 X 30 mL), CH2Cl2
(1 X 30 mL), and H2O (1 X 30 mL). The combined filtrates were washed with
an aqueous solution of NaOH (1M)- (30 mL), and the two phases separated.
The aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 X 30 mL). The combined
organic phases were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated
in vacuo to give 569 mg (80%) of crude 33a as a dark oil
4-[3-(2-Methoxyphenoxy)phenyl]piperazine-1-carboxylic Acid Methyl Ester
(34b). This compound was cleaved from resin 25b (2.48 g, 2.09 mmol) to
give 657 mg (92%) of crude 34b as a dark oil. Purification by
chromatography [heptane → heptane/ EtOAc (3:1)] gave 430 mg (60%) of pale
oil. (LC-MS: UV 73%, ELSD 97%, Rt = 2.94). (LC-MS: UV 100%, ELSD 100%).
1H NMR: δ 7.15 (m, 1H), 7.11 (m, 1H), 6.99 (m, 1H), 6.97 (m, 1H), 6.90
(m, 1H), 6.61 (m, 1H), 6.58 (m, 1H), 6.40 (m, 1H), 3.83 (s, 3H), 3.72 (s,
3H), 3.60 (m, 4H), 3.12 (m, 4H). 13C NMR: δ 158.7, 155.7, 152.4, 151.2,
144.9, 129.7, 124.5, 120.9, 120.8, 112.6, 110.6, 108.6, 105.8, 55.8,
52.5, 48.9, 43.5. HRMALDI-FTMS calcd for C19H22N2O4: m/z 342.1575. Found:
m/z 342.1561. Anal. Calcd for C19H22N2O4: C, 66.65; H, 6.48; N, 8.18.
Found: C, 66.97; H, 6.53; N, 8.07.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical (3rd stage), solid phase, multiple decomplexation cycles
required in 3rd stage, 1,10-phenanthroline soln. prepd. by addn. of MeCN,
H2O, HCl soln., H2O, MeCN, and H2O
