$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for O-arylation of phenol
The phenols (2.21 mmol), CuI (Sigma-Aldrich, 99.999% purity, 0.0147
mmol), TMHD (0.147 mmol), Cs2CO3 (2.94 mmol), the aryl halide (1.47
mmol), and DMF (0.30 mL) were added to a reaction vial and a screw cap
was fitted to it. The reaction mixture was stirred under air in a closed
system at 60°C for 24 h, then the heterogeneous mixture was cooled to RT
and diluted with ethyl acetate. The resulting solution was directly
filtered through a pad of Celite. The combined organic extracts washed
with water twice and the combined organic extracts were dried with
anhydrous Na2SO4 and the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The
crude product was purified by silica-gel column chromatography to afford
the O-arylated product. The identity and purity of all products was
confirmed by 1H and 13C NMR spectroscopic analysis.
1-chloro-3-(m-tolyloxy)benzene6 (3f): Following the general procedure
m-cresol (0.231 ml, 2.21 mmol) and 3-chloroiodobenzene (0.182 ml, 1.47
mmol) provided 295 mg (92% yield) of the coupling product as colourless
oil after purification by flash chromatography (petroleum ether). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.24-7.21 (m, 2H), 7.05 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H),
6.97-6.95 (m, 2H), 6.88 (dd, J = 2.1, 8.1 Hz, 1H), 6.87-6.81 (m, 2H),
2.34 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3): δ = 158.5, 156.3, 140.2, 135.0,
130.4, 129.6, 124.8, 123.0, 120.1, 118.8, 116.6, 116.4, 21.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, aerobic, alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Low catalyst loadings for copper-catalyzed O-arylation of phenols and
heteroaryl halides under mild conditions
